nimchoo downloads place names from GeoNames (https://www.geonames.org) when they are needed, to name climbs and
activities and to say where an activity started (`nch list -v`): the country files and the country outlines from
download.geonames.org.  GeoNames data are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).  They are kept in the cache directory (`data/geonames/`), and the
parts used are in the database; nimchoo itself carries none of them.

The outlines of the countries, used to tell which country a place is in, are Natural Earth's (https://www.naturalearthdata.com),
which is in the public domain; they are downloaded when needed and kept in the cache directory (`data/naturalearth/`).

Map tiles shown by `nch heatmap --web` are loaded by the browser from OpenStreetMap
(c) OpenStreetMap contributors, and Leaflet (BSD 2-Clause) from unpkg.com.
